Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: use the Pro2 reference initiator scan window

The BL616 whitelist initiator defaults to a 60 ms interval and 30 ms window.
Normal Pro2 wake repeatedly reaches a transient connection and then terminates
with HCI reason 0x3e.  The working ESP32-S3 Pro2 bridge uses a 10 ms interval
and a 10 ms window when it issues LE Create Connection.

This change affects only the whitelist LE Create Connection scan cadence.
It does not change the 7.5 ms connection interval, GATT setup, USB reports, or
rumble path.

--- a/components/wireless/bluetooth/blestack/src/host/hci_core.c
+++ b/components/wireless/bluetooth/blestack/src/host/hci_core.c
@@ -1057,9 +1057,12 @@ int bt_le_auto_conn(const struct bt_le_conn_param *conn_param)
 	cp->filter_policy = BT_HCI_LE_CREATE_CONN_FP_WHITELIST;
 	cp->own_addr_type = own_addr_type;
 
-	/* User Initiated procedure use fast scan parameters. */
-	cp->scan_interval = sys_cpu_to_le16(BT_GAP_SCAN_FAST_INTERVAL);
-	cp->scan_window = sys_cpu_to_le16(BT_GAP_SCAN_FAST_WINDOW);
+	/* Match the Pro2 reference bridge's initiator scan cadence.  The stock
+	 * 60 ms / 30 ms whitelist window repeatedly loses synchronization with a
+	 * normally-woken Pro2 on BL616 (0x3e), while the reference central uses a
+	 * continuous 10 ms / 10 ms window. */
+	cp->scan_interval = sys_cpu_to_le16(0x0010);
+	cp->scan_window = sys_cpu_to_le16(0x0010);
 
 	cp->conn_interval_min = sys_cpu_to_le16(conn_param->interval_min);
 	cp->conn_interval_max = sys_cpu_to_le16(conn_param->interval_max);
